From 0eec67588b9123e3bcca0945e923b7ce3cfce6fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:34:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] feat(relayer): Profile H in the signature pre-check
 (lifecycle Level 1, H9)

Decryption Authority Lifecycle draft, Profile H rule H9: advisory prechecks
use the same caps, budget and ordering as the verifiers.

- user_decrypt_signature_check.profile_h (serde default, off): the KMS
  connector's profile_h keys minus the verifier-only H5 and H6. An unknown
  code_first_mode is a configuration error at load.
- Enabled, the v3 pre-check runs the shared crate's
  verify_user_decryption_signature with that policy: H1 caps before any
  read, H2 ordering at one block, H3 budget, and the H4 later-block gate.
- What the pre-check retries is unchanged: transport failures and empty
  reverts within the host-ACL retry window; every other rejection is
  definitive. Shadow differences are logged.
- Disabled, the pre-check is unchanged (verify_signature with
  erc1271_gas_limit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
